  "algorithm_details": {
    "primary": "Find t with d=t^2-residue a quadratic nonresidue, exponentiate (t+sqrt(d))^((p+1)/2) in F_p[sqrt(d)] using pair multiplication, and choose the smaller root.",
    "independent_oracle": "Scan candidates from 0 through p-1 and return the least root found.",
    "complexity": "At most p Legendre-symbol trial checks, each O(log p), followed by O(log p) extension-field multiplications; constant scratch space."
  },
